I don't know if I understand your question.

> Isn't it easier to state that "-ing" attaches to uncertain heads just
like {calonu zo'e} does in Lojban ?

No. The three syntactic structures I describe are independently warranted;
they're not invented just to account for this sentence's ambiguity.
Sometimes syntactically different sentences just happen to have the same
phonology; that's the very definition of ambiguity.

